  "id": "architectural-constraints",
  "term": "architectural constraints",
  "definition": "Architectural constraints are fixed features or limits of a neural network’s structure that could shape how it learns or behaves. In this source, the term is used to contrast structural design requirements with learning effects that can arise on their own from regularities in the training experience.",
